  "term": "dysthymia",
  "definition": "Dysthymia is a long-lasting depressed mood that is present for most of the day on more days than not for at least 2 years, or 1 year in children. It also includes at least two associated problems such as changes in appetite or sleep, low energy, low self-esteem, poor concentration or decision-making, or hopelessness.",
